s>JY</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Lee</surname> <given-names>SH</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Food-borne intestinal trematode infections in the Republic of Korea.</article-title><source>Parasitol Int</source> <year>2002</year>;<volume>51</volume>:<fpage>129</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>54</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1383-5769(02)00008-9</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12113752</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R19"><label>19. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Chai</surname> <given-names>JY</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Han</surname> <given-names>ET</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Guk</surname> <given-names>SM</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Shin</surname> <given-names>EH</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Sohn</surname> <given-names>WM</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Yong</surname> <given-names>TS</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>High prevalence of liver and intestinal fluke infections among residents of Savannakhet Province in Laos.</article-title><source>Korean J Parasitol</source> <year>2007</year>;<volume>45</volume>:<fpage>213</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.3347/kjp.2007.45.3.213</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17876167</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R20"><label>20. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Pearson</surname> <given-names>JC</given-names></string-name> <article-title>A revision of the subfamily Haplorchinae Loss, 1899 (Trematoda: Heterophyinae).</article-title><source>Parasitology</source> <year>1964</year>;<volume>54</volume>:<fpage>604</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>76</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="R21"><label>21. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Eom</surname> <given-names>KS</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Rim</surname> <given-names>HJ</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Jang</surname> <given-names>DH</given-names></string-name> <article-title>A study on the parasitic helminths of domestic duck (<italic>Anas platyrhynchos</italic> var. <italic>domestica Linnaeus</italic>) in Korea.</article-title><source>Korean J Parasitol</source> <year>1984</year>;<volume>22</volume>:<fpage>215</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>21</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>